me{sin}⁡(5x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its minimum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139533795 true] [17592186251657 1113 #uuid "6b7e329d-52d4-572d-bcbe-003c4b6ced95" 13194139533795 true] [17592186251657 1145 "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=5x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate $X$-values at the minima of\n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡X.\n$$\n\nThe $X$-values at the minima are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the $x$-values at the minima of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ 5x+\\frac{\\pi }{2} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ 5x & =-\\pi +2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{5}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the values of $x$ that minimize $f(x)$ are given by $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{5}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{5},$ where $n$ is any integer." 13194139533795 true] [17592186251658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251659 13194139533795 true] [17592186251658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251660 13194139533795 true] [17592186251658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251661 13194139533795 true] [17592186251658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251662 13194139533795 true] [17592186251658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251663 13194139533795 true] [17592186251658 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533795 true] [17592186251658 1041 "selection" 13194139533795 true] [17592186251658 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251663 13194139533795 true] [17592186251658 1110 #uuid "428403ad-1ff6-5fcb-8a18-87e2a3d32520" 13194139533795 true] [17592186251659 1034 "x=\\frac{\\pi }{5}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5}" 13194139533795 true] [17592186251659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533795 true] [17592186251659 1111 #uuid "6c8270af-f37d-5b55-9606-ac2b39fc71ee" 13194139533795 true] [17592186251660 1034 "x=\\frac{\\pi